        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T13:28:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113606,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "<p >Almost all MSAs have arisen in the oral cavity, with palate and buccal mucosa being the most frequently affected subsites. A single case involved the parotid gland {31094920; 32687666; 33982215}. Cases have been reported affecting the skin {35690998}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T15:34:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113607,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a painless, slow-growing mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T13:28:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113608,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fewer than 30&nbsp;cases have been reported. The mean patient age is 49.5&nbsp;years (range: 17&ndash;83&nbsp;years), and there is a slight female predominance {31094920; 32687666; 33982215}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T13:28:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113609,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T13:28:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113610,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p>MSA is characterized by chromosomal rearrangement and fusion of the <em>MEF2C</em> gene (5q14.3) with <em>SS18</em> (18q11.2). Rare reported cases with an alternate fusion <em>SS18</em>::<em>ZBTB7A</em> may represent a different tumour type {36221318; 33982215}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-22T14:24:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113611,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>MSA grossly appears to be a non-ulcerated, well-circumscribed mass. The masses average 11&nbsp;mm (range: 6&ndash;30&nbsp;mm).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T13:28:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113612,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>MSA has very consistent morphological features: (1)&nbsp;a microcystic-predominant growth pattern with occasional cribriform structures or cords; (2)&nbsp;uniform intercalated duct-like tumour cells with attenuated eosinophilic to clear cytoplasm; (3)&nbsp;monotonous oval hyperchromatic nuclei with indistinct nucleoli; (4)&nbsp;abundant basophilic luminal secretions; (5)&nbsp;a variably cellular fibromyxoid stroma; and (6)&nbsp;rounded borders with subtle infiltrative growth into nearby skeletal muscle, fat, or minor salivary glands. Occasionally, MSA is accompanied by pseudoepitheliomatous hyperplasia, tumour-associated lymphoid proliferation, or metaplastic bone formation. Perineural invasion is rare, necrosis is absent, and mitotic rates are low.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>MSA has a consistent immunophenotype. It is positive for S100, SOX10, and p63, and negative for p40, mammaglobin, and calponin. Occasional cases are focally positive for SMA.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Secretory carcinoma has more abundant cytoplasm, pink secretions, mammaglobin positivity, and harbours different fusions (usually <em>ETV6</em>::<em>NTRK3</em>). Polymorphous adenocarcinoma shows more architectural diversity and different genetic alterations (mutations or rearrangements of <em>PRKD1</em>, <em>PRKD2</em>, or <em>PRKD3</em>). Adenoid cystic carcinoma has two cell populations, is far more infiltrative, and harbours rearrangements of <em>MYB</em>, <em>MYBL1</em>, and/or <em>NFIB</em>. Sclerosing microcystic adenocarcinoma is less cellular, with more stroma, more cord-like growth, and a subtly biphasic tumour population.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T13:28:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113613,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "<p>Not reported</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T15:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113614,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>MEF2C</em>::<em>SS18</em> fusion can be demonstrated by RNA sequencing, RT-PCR, or <em>SS18</em> break-apart FISH {31094920; 32687666; 33394377; 33982215}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T13:28:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113615,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> a salivary gland malignancy with a microcystic-predominant growth pattern; bluish secretions; fibromyxoid stroma; monotonous tumour cells; positivity for S100 and p63 but not p40 or mammaglobin.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>SS18</em> rearrangement demonstrated by FISH, RNA sequencing, or PCR (in selected cases).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T15:34:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113616,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "<p>Staging follows the eighth edition of the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC)&nbsp;/ American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-09T16:57:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113617,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 91,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "<p>MSA usually behaves in an indolent manner, with only rare reported cases of distant or regional metastasis {35780228; 36043435}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-22T14:24:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]